## SQ-FSD-01
@group B
@commands Boot a server; read `logs/latest.log`
@pass One `[farmers-donor] N files from Farmer's Structures 1.0.6 {...}` line; no `Could not translate`; the counts list `blocks mapped minecraft:pink_petals`, no `blocks to air` for a block you expect to exist (rope fence, gleaming salad, hanging canvas sign, basket)
@fails donor jar
@draft no batch holds this row yet
## SQ-FSD-02 | no donor jar: one warning, the game loads on Farmer's Structures 1.0.0 data
@group B
@commands Rename the donor jar, boot
@pass One warning that it is missing; the game loads with the 1.0.0 structures only
@fails donor jar
@from batches/r1102b/s3_A2.qb
bootexpect Done \(
bootexpect is missing: Farmer's Structures runs on its installed 1\.0\.0 data
bootreject \[farmers-donor\] \d+ files from Farmer's Structures 1\.0\.6
shell n=$(grep -c "is missing: Farmer's Structures runs on its installed 1.0.0 data" logs/latest.log); echo "warnings: $n"; [ "$n" -eq 1 ]
> forceload add 96 96 127 127
sleep 20
> place structure farmers_structures:cooks 240 -60 600
look the cook house places (1.0.0 pieces only; any "Empty or non-existent pool" line names a 1.0.6 piece)

